  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 152 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThe mid/upper ridge was situated over the Rockies while the ridge \naxis extends ESE across the Southern and portions of the Central \nPlains. This will allow for a persistence type forecast through the \nupcoming week and into the beginning of the weekend with triple \ndigit heat lingering over the area through the period. The heat \nadvisory was upgraded to an excessive heat warning through Friday \nwith multiple consecutive days of triple digit heat indices \nanticipated.\n\nAs move into the day on Thursday, a shortwave trough moving across \nthe Northern Plains may help to drive a frontal boundary southward \ninto northern Kansas. This front could become a focus for showers \nand thunderstorms but confidence in how far south the front \nprogresses remains fairly low at this time. This may bring some \nsubtle relief from the heat for those along the I-70 corridor but \nsouthern Kansas is expected to remain hot. Repeated rounds of \nshowers/storms on Fri-Sat could drive the effective frontal boundary \nfurther southward as we move into the weekend but confidence in how \nfar south remains fairly low.\n\nBy Sunday, the front is progged to move southward near the OK state \nline which is expected to bring some temporary relief from the heat. \nAnother shortwave trough could also bring showers and thunderstorms \nto the area Sunday night into early Monday. The mid/upper ridge is \nprogged to amplify over the Central Plains once again by Tue-Wed \nbringing rising heights/increasing thickness and rising temperatures \nonce again.",
